# Metrics & algorithm explanations

When adding or changing **charts, aggregates, or derived metrics** (journal, calculator, training, theory):

## Mandatory

1. **Document in code** — JSDoc or one-line comment on the pure function stating formula name and what is summed/maximized.
2. **Brief UI copy** — Russian, 1–2 sentences per metric; expandable `<details>` or inline hint near legend/axis (quiet UI, iPhone-safe).
3. **Memory Bank** — if new gold standard: note formulas in matching `memory-bank/reference/*-standard.md`.

## Style

- Name the formula when non-obvious (Epley, Brzycki, tonnage vs reps).
- Say what is compared or scaled (best set per session, last N slots, relative bar height).
- Do **not** duplicate calculator prescription logic in journal copy.

## Canon

- Journal chart: `journalMetrics.ts`, `JournalMetricsHelp.tsx`, `journal-progress-chart-standard.md`
- `memory-bank/systemPatterns.md` — Metrics explanations workflow
- `memory-bank/style-guide.md` — Copy for metrics
